19. Extra details for selected issues

Issue 4 and 11: Captions vs transcripts**
- **Captions:** time-synced text of speech and important sounds, shown with the video.
- **Transcript:** a full text version of audio or video, readable separately.
- **Audio description:** narration of important visual content, for blind users.
- Auto-generated captions must be checked and corrected for accuracy.

Issue 6: Descriptive links**
```html
<!-- Bad -->
<a href="form.pdf">Click here</a>
<!-- Good -->
<a href="form.pdf">Download the 2026 admission form (PDF)</a>
```

Issue 7: Heading hierarchy**
```html
<h1>University Admissions</h1>
  <h2>Undergraduate Programmes</h2>
    <h3>Entry Requirements</h3>
  <h2>Postgraduate Programmes</h2>
```
- Use only one `<h1>` per page and never skip levels (e.g. H2 to H4).
- Choose headings for structure, not for how big the text looks.

Issue 9: Colour alone**
```html
<span class="error">⚠ Error: Enter a valid email address</span>
```
The text and icon carry the message, so colour is only extra help.

Issue 10: Auto-play and flashing**
- Content must not flash more than **three times per second**.
- Any audio that plays for more than 3 seconds must have a pause or mute control.
```html
<video controls muted>...</video>
```

Issue 12: Time limits**
- Warn the user before the session expires and let them extend it (e.g. "Add 5 minutes").
- Exceptions: real-time events such as auctions, or limits that are essential.

Issue 13: Plain language**
- Aim for short sentences (about 15 to 20 words) and short paragraphs.
- Replace jargon: "utilise" becomes "use", "commence" becomes "start".
- Spell out abbreviations the first time (e.g. UCU, Uganda Christian University).

**Issue 15: Reflow**
- Content should work at 320 px width (or 400% zoom) without horizontal scrolling.
- Use relative units (`%`, `rem`) instead of fixed pixels.
```css
img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
```

